quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  20,126,"He will say: ‘This is how it is. Our revelations came to you, but you forgot them. And thus, you are forgotten today.’"
  20,127,"And thus, We recompense the one who exceeds the limits and does not believe in the revelations of his Lord. And indeed, the punishment of the Hereafter is more severe and more lasting."
  20,128,Does it not guide them (to see) how many generations We have destroyed before them in whose dwellings they walk around? There are indeed signs in that for those who possess reason.
  20,129,"Had it not been for a previous word from your Lord and an appointed term (for their punishment), the inevitable (calamity) would have happened."
  20,130,"So be patient with what they say. And glorify the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset. And glorify Him in the hours of the night and at the ends of the day, so that you may be pleased (with the reward)."
  20,131,Do not extend your glance towards what We have provided certain groups of them to enjoy as the splendour of this worldly life so that We may test them through it. And the provision of your Lord (in the Hereafter) is better and more lasting.
  20,132,And command your family for prayer and be steadfast in observing it yourself. We do not ask you for any provision. It is We Who provide for you. And the Ultimate End belongs to God-consciousness.
  20,133,"And they say: ‘Why does he not bring us a (visible) sign from his Lord?’ Has there not come to them a clear proof (i.e. the Qur’an), which is (mentioned) in the earlier Scriptures?"
  20,134,"Had We destroyed them with a punishment before this (revelation), they would certainly have said: ‘Our Lord! Why did You not send a messenger to us, for then we would have followed Your revelations before we became disgraced and humiliated?’"
  20,135,Say (to them): ‘Each (of us) is waiting. So keep waiting! For you will soon come to know who the people of the straight path are and who are rightly guided.’
